{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/mule/ast.ts@L74","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/mule/ast.ts","span":{"start":74,"end":77}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/mule/ast.ts","span":{"start":74,"end":77},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:98026e8e0488e6a1dbc02cff9340b59ad56deaebec2dd40620d4092bb331a77b","meta":{"text":"A DataWeave / expression payload attached to a processor attribute. `raw` is the literal source\n(`#[…]]`); `language` is 'dw2' (Mule 4 DataWeave 2), 'mel' (Mule 3 Mule Expression Language), or\n'unknown'. The raw text may reference property keys (`p('key')`) but never carries resolved\nsecret values."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/mule/ast.ts@L84","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/mule/ast.ts","span":{"start":84,"end":87}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/mule/ast.ts","span":{"start":84,"end":87},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:a38adbe88650690632f8eb025f0563b7bde711771ed22f7f9764078433fc8f36","meta":{"text":"A semantic Mule message processor. `namespace`/`operation` are the element's prefix + local name\n(e.g. `http` + `request`); `semanticKind` classifies it for the graph. Attribute values are\nsanitized: credential-like literals become `<redacted>`, `${key}`/`secure::key` stay as key\nreferences, and DataWeave `#[…]` payloads move to `expressions` (never into `attributes`)."}}
